# Findings this project has looked at and accepted. Anything not listed here
# is reported by `make scan-code` and by CI.
#
# Nothing in this file suppresses a vulnerability. It is misconfiguration
# rules only, and each one needs a reason.

# DS-0002: "Specify at least 1 USER command in Dockerfile with non-root user"
#
# A must-gather image cannot run as a non-root user. It reads /host on the
# node through a privileged debug pod, runs commands against the kubelet, and
# writes into a directory the copy sidecar owns. Upstream's own Dockerfile has
# no USER line either, and adding one would stop the image collecting
# anything.
DS-0002

# KSV-0009, KSV-0014, KSV-0017, KSV-0118, KSV-0121 on
# node-gather/node-gather-ds.yaml
#
# node-gather is upstream's daemonset for reading the nodes themselves: it
# mounts the host filesystem and runs privileged, which is the entire reason
# it exists. A node-gather pod that satisfied these rules could not gather
# anything from a node. The manifest is upstream's and is applied, unchanged,
# by gather_nodes.
KSV-0009
KSV-0014
KSV-0017
KSV-0118
KSV-0121
